Subject: [PATCH] worker: stop rewriting zone.action to CREATE on a NO_ZONE poll

When the zone poll cannot find the expected serial because the nameserver
does not hold the zone at all, ZonePoller._threshold_met() classifies the
result as NO_ZONE rather than ERROR, and _on_failure() then does:

    self.zone.status = error_status          # 'NO_ZONE'
    if error_status == 'NO_ZONE':
        self.zone.action = 'CREATE'

ZonePoller.__call__() immediately calls _update_status(), which hands that
mutated object to UpdateStatus and so calls

    central_api.update_status(ctxt, zone.id, zone.status, zone.serial,
                              zone.action)

with action='CREATE'. Central guards the write with a check that the action
it was handed still matches the action recorded for the zone
(central/service.py update_status):

    if action is None or zone.action == action:
        zone = self._update_zone_or_record_status(zone, status, serial)
    else:
        LOG.debug('Updated action different from current action. '
                  'Keeping current action ...')

For a zone whose stored action is UPDATE -- any zone that has ever had a
recordset added or changed -- 'UPDATE' != 'CREATE', so the else branch is
taken and the status update is silently discarded. Nothing is written, no
error is surfaced, and the zone stays PENDING forever. designate-producer's
PeriodicRecoveryTask then re-queues it every 120s, the poll fails again, and
the zone loops indefinitely.

The rewrite is also redundant. Central already performs exactly this
transition itself, for both actions, in _update_zone_or_record_status:

    elif status == 'NO_ZONE':
        if zone_or_record.action in ['CREATE', 'UPDATE']:
            zone_or_record.action = 'CREATE'
            zone_or_record.status = 'ERROR'

So the worker only needs to report the zone's true current action and let
central decide. Dropping the two lines makes an UPDATE zone match the guard,
reach _update_zone_or_record_status, and land on action=CREATE/status=ERROR
-- which is what the code already intended.

CREATE zones are unaffected: the removed lines assigned 'CREATE' to a zone
whose action was already 'CREATE', so the value sent to central is unchanged.
DELETE zones never reach this branch, because _threshold_met() only returns
NO_ZONE when is_not_delete is true.

Nothing downstream in the worker depends on the mutation. ZoneAction.__call__
branches on self.action, the constructor argument, not self.zone.action, and
parse_query_results() reads zone.action during _do_poll(), which has already
completed by the time _on_failure() runs.

Demonstrated on a deployment whose mdns was not serving, so every poll
returned NO_ZONE. A zone left untouched (action CREATE) reached
CREATE/ERROR in ~2m45s, while an otherwise identical zone with two
recordsets added (action UPDATE) never left PENDING -- 150s of one-second
polling of the zones table showed no state change at all, and 12 minutes of
15-second polling never once observed ERROR.

Still present on designate master as of 960b3b7f, so there is nothing to
backport.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/designate/worker/tasks/zone.py
+++ var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/designate/worker/tasks/zone.py
@@ -555,9 +555,6 @@
 
         self.zone.status = error_status
 
-        if error_status == 'NO_ZONE':
-            self.zone.action = 'CREATE'
-
         return False
 
     def _on_success(self, query_result, status):
